1
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:00,720
The important thing is there?.

2
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:06,117
The reason why it's there is?.

3
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,840
I will protect you!.

4
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:13,377
Okay, let's go ahead and go ahead!.

5
00:01:13,460 --> 00:01:16,300
The moon will always come to the moon!.

6
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:19,837
The moon will come to the moon!.

7
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:22,900
Let's look at the moon?.

8
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:55,960
Ha-ha-ha!

9
00:01:56,180 --> 00:01:57,920
We're almost to the exit now!

10
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:00,551
Full speed ahead until we fly out of here!

11
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:01,870
What?

12
00:02:01,953 --> 00:02:02,783
No way!

13
00:02:02,866 --> 00:02:03,696
You're getting right!

14
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:25,320
All right, there it is!

15
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:26,814
Time to move out, men!

16
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:30,680
Let's charge ahead, join them,
and get Franky back! Yeah!

17
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:35,040
City! Gomorrah! Jump!

18
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:42,650
Straw Hat!

19
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:48,220
The entire Franky family
thanks you for helping us!

20
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:50,260
We'll never forget it!

21
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:53,860
Fire the connection cannon!

22
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:06,210
Cool!

23
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,480
Hey, nice job!

24
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,037
Pretty high-class bullets you got there!

25
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:11,950
Awesome!

26
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:16,037
Damn it!

27
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,296
You stupid bastards!

28
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:20,076
You idiot, you gotta be more careful!

29
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:27,020
Ah, looks like it drifted a bit, huh?

30
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:31,280
Listen, I know these sea trains
like the back of my hand.

31
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:32,813
I'll find that railway.

32
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:40,260
Found ya! Let's go!

33
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,350
Attention!

34
00:03:44,433 --> 00:03:46,357
This train will soon be on the railway!

35
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:50,100
Once we are our acceleration
will increase exponentially.

36
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:54,517
Find something to hold on to so we
can keep the injuries to a minimum.

37
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,776
A minimum will be injured regardless?

38
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:07,180
Listen, you!

39
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:09,160
Behave yourself! Whoa!

40
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,913
That was close, Granny!

41
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,337
A little to the right!

42
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:13,250
Yeah!

43
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:15,100
Don't you worry.

44
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,517
I'll get it right next time.

45
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:17,800
You'll see. Huh?

46
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:20,340
Chisney! Candy!

47
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:22,830
No!

48
00:04:22,913 --> 00:04:24,200
I left you with iceberg!

49
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:31,386
How could this have happened?

50
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,637
Get out from there and come inside!

51
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:35,544
You'll be blown away out there!

52
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:38,020
We're fine! We're fine!

53
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:42,010
Candy!

54
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:43,780
Ha-ha-ha!

55
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:45,220
I'm gonna fall!

56
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:49,200
Whatever you do, don't let go! I'm flying!

57
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:52,510
Wait!

58
00:04:52,593 --> 00:04:53,853
Hold on a second, okay?

59
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:55,260
Let me slow down!

60
00:05:00,420 --> 00:05:01,250
Huh?

61
00:05:01,333 --> 00:05:03,040
Oh, no! I forgot!

62
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:04,680
No brakes!

63
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:05,680
We can't stop!

64
00:05:09,020 --> 00:05:10,340
Whoa, what the heck?

65
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:12,097
Hey, that kind of looks like fun!

66
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:13,010
Ha!

67
00:05:13,093 --> 00:05:15,180
Look, it's the Straw Hat guy! Hey!

68
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:17,750
Hurry!

69
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:20,136
Grab those two and bring them inside!

70
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:23,554
Once this train hits the
railway, they'll be blown away!

71
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,070
Right!

72
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:30,560
No! No!

73
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:03,920
I thought I was a goner!

74
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,460
You almost were!

75
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:09,820
I said, if you don't come inside,
you're gonna get blown away!

76
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:14,700
Oh, that speed was crazy. Told ya.

77
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,628
He's right, that was rough.

78
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:18,380
Oh, hurt my back.

79
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:20,500
Hold on a second.

80
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:23,357
There are a few more people
in here than there should be.

81
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:24,270
Yeah?

82
00:06:24,353 --> 00:06:25,183
Who do you mean?

83
00:06:25,266 --> 00:06:26,096
He means you!

84
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:27,220
I mean you, too!

85
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:33,920
I tried, but no matter what I
said or did, I couldn't stop you.

86
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:37,297
And the enemy that you'd go
through all of this to rescue your

87
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:40,968
friend from is the exact same
one that tried to kill Iceberg.

88
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:46,840
I've got a word or two of my own I want
to say to those bastards. Ha ha ha! Yeah!

89
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:48,820
You're not the only one!

90
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:51,997
We figured that if we snuck
onto the train and followed you,

91
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:55,637
we'd be right behind you when things
went down with those Newgate assassins!

92
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:56,602
So here we are.

93
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:58,457
Seems our hunch was right.

94
00:06:58,540 --> 00:06:59,560
Let us join you.

95
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:01,620
We want to avenge Iceberg.

96
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:04,097
Sounds like we all have a common enemy.

97
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:06,657
They're the same ones that
kidnapped our bro Franky!

98
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:07,760
Yeah, he's right.

99
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:09,257
No point in playing dumb.

100
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:10,837
We know exactly who they are.

101
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:11,840
Hey, Galley-La!

102
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:15,237
If anything happens to him,
it's gonna be on your shoulders.

103
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,150
Can it.

104
00:07:16,233 --> 00:07:18,645
Iceberg's the one that's
endured the most here.

105
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:19,930
Hey!

106
00:07:20,013 --> 00:07:21,197
What the heck are they talking about?

107
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:22,110
Come on!

108
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:24,237
There's something you're
not telling us, Paulie!

109
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,677
Yeah, it's time to come clean.

110
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:26,777
Tell us everything.

111
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:27,980
We need answers.

112
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:30,301
You know who the true culprit is.

113
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:31,957
We're not stupid, you know.

114
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:34,157
We got a pretty good idea who it is.

115
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:35,946
You're not gonna surprise us.

116
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:41,740
Well, I guess the story about them
disappearing was too convenient.

117
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,940
Fine, I'll tell you.

118
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:47,380
The true identities of those masked men

119
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:52,600
are Luchi, Kaku, Khalifa,
and Bluno from the bar.

120
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:54,220
It was them.

121
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:57,120
They're the ones who
tried to kill Iceberg.

122
00:07:58,820 --> 00:08:01,517
Are you telling me you
never even thought of them?

123
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:03,897
You said they went back to their hometown.

124
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:05,237
Come on, you believe that?

125
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:08,397
We thought it was Michael and
Hoykel from the Backstreet District.

126
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:09,310
Roar!

127
00:08:09,393 --> 00:08:10,223
Roar!

128
00:08:10,306 --> 00:08:11,136
Who the hell are they?

129
00:08:11,219 --> 00:08:12,049
What?

130
00:08:12,132 --> 00:08:12,962
You're kidding.

131
00:08:13,045 --> 00:08:13,875
You've never heard of them?

132
00:08:13,958 --> 00:08:14,788
They're pretty famous in the Backstreet.

133
00:08:14,871 --> 00:08:15,701
Roar! Roar!

134
00:08:15,784 --> 00:08:18,197
Why would half the foreman
leave in the middle of a crisis?

135
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:20,000
That really hit the spot.

136
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:21,580
Man, I was starving.

137
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:25,660
Right. So,

138
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:28,757
even though we got in a few
fights back in town with

139
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:32,237
both the Franky family and
with the Galley-La shipwrights,

140
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:35,237
the enemy we're all going
after here is one and the same.

141
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:38,517
Now, the strongest one, the
toughest out of all of them,

142
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,337
is definitely that pigeon guy.

143
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:41,250
He's mine.

144
00:08:41,333 --> 00:08:43,157
I'm going to beat the crap out of him.

145
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:44,070
Luffy's right.

146
00:08:44,153 --> 00:08:46,217
This is a battle to get
back what those four

147
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:48,517
goons from the world
government took from us.

148
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:52,620
So, we either reach them in time
or all of this will be for nothing.

149
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:55,200
Granny, look!

150
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:56,660
It's Akula Call!

151
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,580
It's here already?

152
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:01,780
Hey, let me take a look.

153
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,330
Oh no!

154
00:09:08,413 --> 00:09:10,697
Hey, shouldn't you be in
the engine room right now?

155
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:14,074
You've got to find some way
to dodge that gigantic wave!

156
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:15,210
Uh-uh!

157
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:17,717
Rocket Man can't be controlled, remember?

158
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:21,940
We can't adjust the speed, use
the brakes, or change our course.

159
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:25,937
My job ended as soon as I
got us up on the railway.

160
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:29,077
Trains lined up on the
tracks, running at full speed,

161
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:31,866
and there's nothing
anybody can do to stop it!

162
00:09:32,340 --> 00:09:33,170
No.

163
00:09:33,253 --> 00:09:37,380
Hey, if we don't do something
and fast, this train's gonna...

164
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:44,000
Everybody on this train
has the exact same goal.

165
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:46,613
There's no point in fighting separately.

166
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:49,040
Yeah, he's right.

167
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:53,580
From this point forward, we fight as one.

168
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,937
There are two more of my
crew on that other train.

169
00:09:57,020 --> 00:10:01,196
Once we've caught up to them, our
fighting force will be even stronger.

170
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:04,560
Listen up!

171
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:07,447
We're not going to let
that big wave beat us!

172
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:09,440
We will achieve our goal!

173
00:10:10,220 --> 00:10:11,180
Let's go!

174
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:21,480
All right, boys, why don't you show me what
you can do about that wave? You got it!

175
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:22,740
Fire all cannons!

176
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,980
Blow it to man! Rawr!

177
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:26,980
Turn it to my special tank!

178
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:28,480
It's just water!

179
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:30,340
Don't be afraid, bros!

180
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:32,580
Prepare the cannon! Roger!

181
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:36,100
Get a move on!

182
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:50,940
Oh, the transponder snail's ringing.

183
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:08,800
Hey, you there?

184
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,620
Yes, Captain T-Bone.

185
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:14,120
How did you get that
injury on your arm? Huh?

186
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:16,620
Oh. This?

187
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:19,937
I got bitten by a bug earlier,
and it bled when I scratched it.

188
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:20,850
How awful!

189
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:23,006
We must staunch the bleeding.

190
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:26,322
We'll have to make do with this.

191
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:29,481
Sir, you don't have to
tear your cape just for me.

192
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:32,657
It may be your arm that's bleeding.

193
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:36,857
But when one of my men is injured,
It's my heart that hurts the most.

194
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:39,060
Captain, thank you!

195
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:44,137
Let us fill today and every
day forth With good deeds!

196
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:46,720
So that peace and kindness shall reign.

197
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:52,080
This race is still really scary?

198
00:11:52,780 --> 00:11:53,610
Captain!

199
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:54,860
I'll help.

200
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:57,277
Oh, good.

201
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:58,917
But let me explain the problem.

202
00:11:59,000 --> 00:11:59,830
first.

203
00:11:59,913 --> 00:12:04,560
If there's anything I can do, even
if it kills me, I will protect you.

204
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:07,720
Aw, thanks.

205
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:11,240
But the problem is with the
officials at Car 6 and 7.

206
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:13,244
They were completely wiped out.

207
00:12:13,460 --> 00:12:17,166
Not only that, the two criminals
detained in Car 6 are missing.

208
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:18,440
That's awful!

209
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:22,077
We can't tell if the
prisoners escaped on their

210
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:24,557
own or if they were helped
by an unknown intruder.

211
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:27,357
For heaven's sake, man,
start a rescue operation.

212
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:29,877
Help the injured and spread
the word to the other cause.

213
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:30,790
Yes, sir.

214
00:12:32,580 --> 00:12:33,410
Nami.

215
00:12:33,493 --> 00:12:34,740
Nami, can you hear me? Yeah.

216
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,317
What's going on, Sanji?

217
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,880
I've got some bad news.

218
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:40,044
Things have gotten complicated.

219
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:41,500
What do you mean?

220
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:43,840
Hey, wait a sec.

221
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:45,256
What was that noise?

222
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:47,654
Is someone there with you or something?

223
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:50,920
It's nothing.

224
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:53,960
Just some dumbass. Huh? Say what?

225
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:56,840
Sanji, what's that noise?

226
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:58,777
Sounds like a bunch of screaming.

227
00:12:58,860 --> 00:12:59,917
Are you OK over there?

228
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,647
What do you mean by dumbass?

229
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:04,000
Sorry, dumbass is actually.

230
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,230
Roar!

231
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:07,550
Roar!

232
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:08,660
Jimmy Turner!

233
00:13:13,320 --> 00:13:14,150
Roar!

234
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,620
Leave it to us!

235
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:19,600
Not even making a dent.

236
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:21,040
I should've figured.

237
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:23,217
You think those puny
things are gonna work?

238
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:25,000
Everybody step back!

239
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:28,760
Let the Franky family's
special cannon do its stuff!

240
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:30,760
Target!

241
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:32,280
Aqua Laguna!

242
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:34,290
Go!

243
00:13:34,373 --> 00:13:35,980
Super Scrap Cannon fire!

244
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:46,360
Fire again! Don't let him!

245
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:55,940
Bring more cannonballs!
Got it! Aim at the center!

246
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:58,340
Focus on one spot! Focus, focus!

247
00:13:58,580 --> 00:13:59,756
Give it all you got!

248
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:02,429
Yeah, good luck with that.

249
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:07,325
By the way, the tracks do rise up a bit,
but not enough to get us over that wave.

250
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:12,502
Rocket Man has done pretty well out here
so far, but if we get hit, we're finished.

251
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:14,919
Does that mean we're all gonna die?

252
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:17,060
No guarantees.

253
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:19,048
I warned you now, didn't I?

254
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:22,710
What?

255
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:24,260
I don't want to die!

256
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:26,340
I see.

257
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:28,060
They still have Robin.

258
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:33,376
Sounds like things are pretty
lively on your end, too.

259
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:35,240
Hey, listen, Sanji.

260
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:38,720
I need to tell you why
Robin's doing all this.

261
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:41,841
And also why everyone's
screaming for that matter.

262
00:14:43,060 --> 00:14:44,000
Shut up!

263
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:50,400
So, like I was just saying, we
found out why Robin's with CP9.

264
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:53,937
We're out here trying to follow her,
but things are kind of crazy right now.

265
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:55,100
It's a long story.

266
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:58,520
We're all gonna die!

267
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:00,420
But I don't wanna die!

268
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:01,740
Me either!

269
